            <ArticleTitle>[Pain complaints in a patient with schizophrenia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>318-322</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Schizophrenia is a complex pathology. Its prevalence reaches almost 1 %. Its semiology can be diversified. Sensorial perception can be altered included pain perception. Most of the studies conclude that psychotic patients have a hypoalgesia. It's important to consider this fact to avoid missing potentially grave somatic disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
